= jesp/encoder: the strict-refusal campaign (NQP_CODE_STRICT) to green
NQP_CODE_STRICT=1 makes an encoder refusal a hard error naming the block and op, not a silent
bytecode fallback; the nqp bootstrap builds green under it: falsey, stringify/intify/numify,
pre/postinc/dec, the dispatcher register/delegate/track/guard desugars, savecapture (31), nqp::for
as FORLOOP (32), indexingoptimized; AttrSite keys on class handle and attribute name. Fixed on the
strict-green build: getlexdyn walks from the current frame, throw and loop controls force a frame,
repeat's body inside the loop Block, an untyped if/ternary takes its arms' common type, hllizeIn.
- 9d3981e9d WIP jesp/encoder: strict-refusal campaign (NQP_CODE_STRICT), 11 ops, for in progress
- 51c45a5fe jesp/encoder: strict-refusal campaign green -- for, postinc/postdec, indexingoptimized; AttrSite keyed by name
- 2148ee5c1 jesp/encoder+runtime: first runtime regressions of the strict-green build
- 5aeb58b15 jesp/encoder: an untyped if/ternary takes its arms' common type, as Compiler.nqp does
- 156e55e93 runtime: hllize's transform road takes the block's language, not the frame's

= jesp/encoder+engine: custom_args blocks on the engine
The encoder's verdict line is a class method Compiler.nqp calls for the custom_args bypass, so a
census counts every block; the 60000-char program gate applies to the string-constant road only,
not the LZ4 sidecar. Then the bypass goes: P6BINDSIG (33) binds through RakOps.p6bindsig over the
frame's own csd/args and returns from the program when the binder auto-threaded a Junction;
P6TRYBINDSIG (34) answers 1/0 for the assertparamcheck around it; patch_params emits an empty
header (required 0, accepted -1) for such a block so the arity check still stores csd/args.
- 9f39e00b6 jesp/encoder: verdicts for custom_args blocks; no size gate on the sidecar road
- 112b1649c jesp/encoder+engine: custom_args blocks on the engine (P6BINDSIG, P6TRYBINDSIG)
